---
/**
 * Light docs by default (round 2 spec §4.4, R2-9; docs-light.md §4; #454). The reader's choice
 * from the theme toggle (ThemeSelect.astro) is kept under Starlight's own key, `starlight-theme`;
 * the operating system's preference is not followed, so every reader first meets the reference part
 * of the site on paper (a dark-OS reader would otherwise never see the "different part" signal).
 * Blocked storage falls back to light. Inlined so the theme is set before first paint. Starlight's
 * Page.astro server-renders data-theme="dark", so a visit with scripting off keeps today's dark
 * docs, and the toggle hides itself then (starlight.css).
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    let stored = null;
    try {
      stored = localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme');
    } catch {
      // Storage blocked: the default stands.
    }
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme =
      stored === 'dark' ? 'dark' : 'light';
  })();
</script>
